## Context
DESIGN.md §4 PR-6, honoring D6 (first-with-text) and R24's prerequisite.
Verified at edf2748: extraction concatenates attachment texts and keeps only
the joined content, destroying the offset->attachment mapping and the
per-attachment totals a page estimate needs. The PR: keep per-attachment
totalChars/totalPages; deterministic first-with-text (ascending dateAdded, key
tie-break, must appear in the fulltext census); skipped attachments get a
stored reason ("identical text, suppressed" / "different text, not indexed
under first-with-text"). Convergent when a later extraction changes the choice
function's output.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] per-attachment totals recorded, no concatenation across attachments
- [ ] deterministic first-with-text with stored skip reasons
- [ ] PR opened upstream; outcome recorded here

## Amendments (implementation review, 2026-08-26)
Largest pre-query PR in the train (~600+ lines): per-attachment provenance
ripples through ChunkRecord (backend.ts:32-39), both backends' putPassage, the
passages schema (the first real SCHEMA_VERSION bump — hence Blocked-by 0015),
and the memory backend's snapshot. Split into (a) per-attachment records +
totals, (b) first-with-text policy + stored skip reasons. Sequenced before
0019: both rewrite fulltext-source.ts:119-146.
